MiOS Hypr3D supersampling and live-wallpaper wrap. The scene renders at
render.scale x the output (default 2, clamped 1..4 and capped by the GL
texture/renderbuffer/viewport limits and a 768 MiB scene budget) and is
box-filtered down in the composite (one bilinear tap at 1x/2x, N^2 taps
otherwise); FXAA/CAS run on the output grid; pixel-sized glass terms and
grid lines keep their output-pixel size. The live wallpaper wraps ONCE
around the horizon (world.live_wrap = "mirror": centre ahead, mirrored back
half, no seam; "repeat": one copy over 360 degrees) instead of three axis
projections that each showed the whole image; elevation is rectilinear with
the image aspect and the caps fade to the edge row's ring average. One
shared function serves the dome and glass reflections; file panoramas and
panorama_mirror are unchanged. player.look_yaw/look_pitch set an absolute
look (automation/tests); the status dump reports the effective scene size.
Applies after hypr3d-mios-render-quality.patch.

